Local modifications
-------------------

Relative to upstream commit e991466, the following files were changed. No
other file in this directory differs from upstream.

REST API (to serve the SecureScope `vulntracker-ui` frontend)

  web/cves/resources.py
      - Added `apply_cve_ordering()`: honours a `sort` query parameter for
        `updated_at` / `created_at`, and adds a `cvss` sort that annotates
        the queryset with the best available CVSS score, preferring
        v4.0 > v3.1 > v3.0 > v2.0 and defaulting to 0.0.
      - `CveViewSet.get_queryset()` routes through that ordering helper
        instead of the fixed `-updated_at` ordering.
      - Set `permission_classes = [AllowAny]` on the Cve, Weakness, Vendor,
        VendorCve, Product, ProductCve and WeaknessCve view sets, making
        those read-only endpoints reachable without authentication.
        *** This is a deliberate relaxation of upstream's access control.
        Do not expose this instance publicly without restoring it. ***

  web/cves/serializers.py
      - `CveListSerializer` additionally returns `metrics` and `vendors`,
        so the dashboard can render severity and vendor data from the list
        endpoint without an extra round trip per CVE.

  web/opencve/conf/base.py
      - Added `corsheaders` to INSTALLED_APPS and `CorsMiddleware` to
        MIDDLEWARE; set `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS = ["http://localhost:3000"]`
        and `CORS_ALLOW_CREDENTIALS = True` for the local Next.js frontend.
      - Changed the default `DATABASE_URL` to a local Postgres DSN.

  web/opencve/conf/__init__.py
      - Added (empty package marker).

Local development plumbing

  docker/docker-compose.yaml       Publish Postgres on host port 5432.
  docker/docker-compose.dev.yaml   Added.
  docker-compose.dev.yml           Added — standalone Postgres + Redis style
